==Acquisition==
The mod can be bought from [[Son]] for {{sc|20,000}} after reaching '''Rank 3 - Associate''' with the [[Entrati]].

==Notes==
*Clones will attack enemies whether or not {{M|Assault Mode}} or {{M|Elusive Posture}} are equipped. However, [[Posture Mod]] bonuses (e.g. {{D|Puncture}} from {{M|Protector Posture}}) still apply.
*Clones are counted as companions, and will benefit from companion bonuses such as {{M|Summoner's Wrath}} and {{Arcane|Theorem Infection}}.
*Clones will '''not''' enter the [[Rift]].
*Since clone creation requires {{Stat|Energy}} spent, this mod cannot be triggered by {{WF|Hildryn}} or {{WF|Lavos}}.
*The following counts towards the "energy spent" requirement: 
**Energy removed by the Energy Drain modifier in [[Nightmare Mode|Nightmare]] missions.
**Energy drained by {{M|Quick Thinking}} and {{M|Gladiator Finesse}}.
**Energy removed by losing {{Arcane|Arcane Battery}} buff.
**{{WF|Hildryn}} picking up [[File:IconEnergy.gif]][[Energy Orb]]s.
**[[Operator]] casting abilities.
**Channeled and drain-on-use abilities like {{WF|Wisp}}'s {{A|Sol Gate}} and {{WF|Ivara}}'s {{A|Artemis Bow}}.
*Clones are completely invulnerable to any form of damage, and can only die after their listed lifespan has elapsed since they were created.
**Despite being invincible, enemies will still have their aggro drawn to them and attempt to fight them. 
*Cloned [[Sentinels]] will float toward enemies rather than sticking to the player, drawing some aggro away from the player as a result. 
*[[Invisibility]] applied to the player is only shared with the main Companion, it is '''not''' applied to any summoned/spawned clones and they will remain visible to distract enemy fire.
*Since the clones can only use basic attacks, they benefit greatly from [[Beast Claws Mods]]. They can use all the claw mods and deal full damage with them. 
*While clones cannot activate any abilities, they can still be useful for spreading status effects, especially if buffed by external sources (e.g. {{A|Nourish}}).
*Clones will not benefit from, nor trigger, most mods on the Companion itself. Tested examples include but are not limited to: {{M|Momentous Bond}}, {{M|Astral Bond}}, {{M|Vicious Bond}}, {{M|Contagious Bond}}, {{M|Seismic Bond}}, {{M|Tandem Bond}}, {{M|Hunter Recovery}}, {{M|Synth Deconstruct}}, {{M|Fired Up}}, {{M|Hunter Recovery}}, and {{M|Energy Generator}}.
**{{M|Hard Engage}} is an exception, as [[MOA (Companion)]] clones will gain the ability to use melee attacks.
*This mod cannot be equipped on {{Companion|Venari}}.
*Spectral colors of the clones' appearance are dependent on the sentinel's weapon colors.

==Bugs==
* Using the Arsenal in the simulacrum may cause the mod to cease functioning.
* After a host migration, pet clones created by other clients (excluding the new host) lose their invulnerability, appear without cosmetics and with an invisible head.
** Unlike regular clones, they will not disappear after 30 seconds.
** After being downed, these pet clones are able to be revived. The revive marker appears when the player is not looking in the downed clone's direction. No timer or revive progress is shown when reviving.
** These clones do not count towards the 3 clone limit.

